# Reuse Existing Components

Before creating any new component, **always check the catalog below first**. These are the shared components actively used across the running application.

## Rules

1. **Check below before building.** Every component listed here is already in use — reuse it.
2. **Compose, don't duplicate.** Prefer wrapping or extending an existing component over creating a parallel one.
3. **Ask permission.** If no existing component fits, **stop and ask the user for explicit permission** before creating a new one. Explain why.
4. **Document the gap.** When proposing a new component, state which existing ones were considered and why they don't fit.
5. **Match the Mosaic template design.** If a new component is approved, it **must** follow the same visual design language as the existing Mosaic template used throughout this application — same color palette (violet accents, gray tones), same spacing/padding conventions, same border-radius and shadow styles, same dark mode support, same Tailwind CSS utility patterns, and same Headless UI / Radix UI primitives. New components must look like they belong in this app, not like they came from a different design system.

